{"id":2279,"date":"2016-11-17T21:29:27","date_gmt":"2016-11-18T02:29:27","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=2279"},"modified":"2016-11-17T21:29:27","modified_gmt":"2016-11-18T02:29:27","slug":"old-country-inn-pizza-to-die-for","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2016\/11\/17\/old-country-inn-pizza-to-die-for\/","title":{"rendered":"Old Country Inn &#8211; Pizza To Die For"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Kathy and I took a short day trip over to Pine, Arizona today to visit some of their antique, art, and &#8220;junk&#8221; shops and have lunch out. \u00a0We drove through Pine when we went to Payson a few weeks ago, but didn&#8217;t take the opportunity to stop and look around in Pine on that trip.<\/p>\n<p>One of our friends here at the park told us about the fantastic wood-fired pizza at the &#8220;<a href=\"http:\/\/www.oldcountyinn.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">Old Country Inn<\/a>&#8220;. \u00a0 We owe them a thank you for their referral.<\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"  wp-image-2294 alignright\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-33-35.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-33-35\" width=\"346\" height=\"195\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-33-35.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-33-35-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-33-35-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-33-35-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 346px) 100vw, 346px\" \/>It was fantastic, well worth the 45 minute drive over to enjoy the wonderful &#8220;Lefty&#8221; pizza while sitting at the counter just feet away from the wood-fired pizza oven. <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"  wp-image-2301 alignleft\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-08-52.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-08-52\" width=\"394\" height=\"222\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-08-52.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-08-52-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-08-52-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-08-52-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 394px) 100vw, 394px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>We watched the pizza master make our pie and slide it gingerly into just the right spot in the 550 degree oven. \u00a0We could feel the heat radiate from the opening and watch the flames dance across the logs as our lunch was gently bubbling from the heat.<\/p>\n<p>We ordered the &#8220;Lefty&#8221; (<strong>woodfired roasted chicken, roasted red onions, lefty bbq sauce, wisconsin cheddar + cilantro serrano pesto<\/strong>).<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/www.oldcountyinn.com\/#menu\" target=\"_blank\">Here&#8217;s a link to their menu<\/a><\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_2304\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-2304\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2304\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-12-40.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-12-40\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-12-40.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-12-40-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-12-40-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-12-40-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-2304\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The 12-14 inch &#8220;Lefty&#8221; pizza (yummy)<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_2311\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-2311\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2311\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-29-19.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-29-19\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-29-19.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-29-19-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-29-19-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-29-19-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-2311\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">They can serve 8 different craft beers at any one time and easily change the label on the wall<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>They also serve a number of craft beers on tap and have &#8220;The Tap Room&#8221; featuring more craft beers and wine along with small plates a tasting room in a separate building just a few feet from the main restaurant.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_2326\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-2326\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2326\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-35-15.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-35-15\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-35-15.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-35-15-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-35-15-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-35-15-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-2326\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The &#8220;Tap Room&#8221;<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>All in all, it was a great day for a drive in the country (about 45 minutes from Camp Verde to Pine), spending some time in antique shops, and enjoying a great meal crafted with care by a talented chef. \u00a0We definitely recommend &#8220;The Country Inn&#8221; to anyone we know in the area.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_2334\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-2334\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-2334\" src=\"\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-30-511.jpg\" alt=\"2016-11-17-13-30-51\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-30-511.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-30-511-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-30-511-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/11\/2016-11-17-13-30-511-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-2334\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Affordable lunch<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Kathy and I took a short day trip over to Pine, Arizona today to visit some of their antique, art, and &#8220;junk&#8221; shops and have lunch out. \u00a0We drove through Pine when we went to Payson a few weeks ago, but didn&#8217;t take the opportunity to stop and look around in Pine on that trip. &hellip; <a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2016\/11\/17\/old-country-inn-pizza-to-die-for\/\" class=\"more-link\">Continue reading <span class=\"screen-reader-text\">Old Country Inn &#8211; Pizza To Die For<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","pi